   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the navigation law, in relation to the placement of navigational aids adjacent to real property designated as \"Coney Island\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S6032",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6032-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §35, Nav L",
    "lawSection": "Navigation Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6032\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the navigation law, in relation to the placement of\nnavigational aids adjacent to real property designated as \"Coney\nIsland\"\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to protect swimmers from motorized boats\nand jetskis that\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nThis bill would amend Subdivision 2 of section 35 of the navigation\nlaw, as amended by chapter 659 of the laws of 1990, to allow for the\nrequirement of placing aids to navigation in the navigable waters\nadjacent to all real property designated as \"Coney Island\" including\nBrighton Beach.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nSwimmers swimming in beaches in Coney Island and Brighton Beach are at\nrisk of being injured by small boats and jet skis that are prevalent\nin the area, particularly in the summer months. In order to protect\nswimmers and those driving personal watercraft, aids to navigation\nshould be placed five hundred feet from the shoreline, creating a\nsafety zone between such aids and the shoreline, in which no public or\npleasure vehicle shall be permitted to travel.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew Legislation\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nTo be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "printNo": "S6032",
    "publishDate": "2017-05-10",
