    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Parks",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6032A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act relating to the placement of navigational aids adjacent to real\nproperty designated as \"Coney Island\"\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to protect swimmers from jet skis.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nThis bill would authorize the Commissioner of the Office of Parks,\nRecreation and Historic Preservation to install navigational devices\nmarking 500 feet from any designated bathing beach in Coney Island to\ndeter personal watercraft.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nSwimmers swimming in beaches in Coney Island and Brighton Beach are at\nrisk of being injured by jet skis that are prevalent in the area,\nparticularly in the summer months. In order to protect swimmers and\nthose driving personal watercraft, aids to navigation should be placed\nfive hundred feet from the shoreline, creating a safety zone between\nsuch aids and the shoreline, in which no personal watercraft shall be\npermitted to travel.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nThis is new legislation.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS :\n\nNone to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
